package wasi:io@0.2.0;

// Vendored subset of wasi:io/poll@0.2.0 — the `pollable` resource
// (`block` + `[resource-drop]pollable`), which the wasm backend uses to
// wait for a wasi:sockets `tcp-socket.accept` to become ready, plus the
// top-level `poll` multiplexer.
//
// `poll` is what the self-host wasm backend's wasm_poll lowers to
// (#4316). It has to be declared here even though the NATIVE backend
// emits the same import: native never runs wasm-tools, composing in Go
// instead (component.ClassifyCore -> component.Compose) and hand-writing
// the canonical-ABI adapters, so it resolves the import without any WIT.
// The self-host path goes through `wasm-tools component embed` +
// `component new`, which resolves imports against THIS file — and a
// list-typed import cannot be inferred from the core signature alone, so
// omitting it fails the compose with "import interface
// wasi:io/poll@0.2.0 is missing function poll that is required by the
// module".
//
// Source: https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-io
interface poll {
    resource pollable {
        block: func();
    }

    poll: func(in: list<borrow<pollable>>) -> list<u32>;
}
